WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.320
How do we solve a system of linear equations

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.160
using matrices and determinants?

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.900
How do we solve for the values of X and Y here?

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.220
So one way is by solving them using one of the

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.260
regular techniques we have seen.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.340
Or we can use matrices to solve them.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.000
Yes matrices!

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.520
To solve the equations using matrices and determinants

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.540
we first need to write them in the matrix form.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.760
So we first write the matrix of the coefficients.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.480
For the first equation, the coefficients are two and minus one.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.560
And for the second, the coefficients are three and two.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.340
This is the matrix of coefficients of the two variables.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.960
And this will be multiplied with the matrix

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.360
which has the column of variables.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.900
The variables are X and Y.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.500
So a matrix with the coefficients,

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.740
multiplied with a matrix with a column of variables.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.520
And this product is equal to a matrix

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.600
with a column of the constants on the right hand side.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.360
That will be 4 and 13.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.520
This is the matrix form of the above system of equations.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.540
Why do we say that this is the matrix form?

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.240
We will know why when we multiply these two matrices.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.080
Do you remember multiplication of matrices?

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.080
To know if two matrices can be multiplied,

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.260
we need to check their order.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.260
The order of this matrix is two by two,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.040
and that of this one is two by one.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.960
Two rows two columns and two rows one column.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.780
As the second and the third numbers are the same,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.660
these matrices are compatible for multiplication.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.800
The order of the resulting matrix

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.660
will be the first number by the fourth number.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.880
It will be two by one.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.760
So we multiply the first row of this matrix

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.900
with the first column of this matrix and write the product here.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.900
And then multiply the second row of this matrix

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.340
with the first column of this matrix and write the product here.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.720
What will be the product of these two?

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.920
It will be '2x minus y'.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.700
And the product of these two will be '3x plus 2y'.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.660
This is the product of these two matrices.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.620
And this matrix will be written as is.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.420
Now you see why this is the matrix form of the system of equations.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.880
As these two matrices are equal,

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.820
we can say that '2x minus y' will equal 4.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.180
And '3x plus 2y' will equal 13.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.640
Same as these two equations!

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.100
But let's come back to the important point.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:41.480
How does writing it in matrix form help us solve the equations?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.940
Let's see that on the right hand side.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.200
This can be written as 'A times X' is equal to B.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.640
We have called this one matrix A.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:54.240
and this matrix X and this matrix B.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.080
'A times X' is equal to B.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.040
What we're interested in is matrix X.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.820
That will give us the values of variables X and Y.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.080
So to get X on the left hand side,

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.200
we multiply both sides with A inverse.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.240
We get the left hand side as 'A inverse times AX'.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.680
And the right hand side as 'A inverse times B'.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.880
Now 'A inverse times A' will equal the identity matrix.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.360
We get this!

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.300
And we know that the 'identity matrix times any matrix'

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.500
will give us that same matrix.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.900
So the left hand side will equal matrix X.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.000
And the right hand side will be 'A inverse times matrix B'.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.480
That's how we get matrix X.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.760
We multiply 'A inverse with B'.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.080
So when we are given the two equations,

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.840
we write it in this form, find the inverse of this matrix,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.380
and multiply it with this to get matrix X.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:55.940
And that will give us the values of the variables.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:59.000
We will solve this example in the next lesson.

